{
  "id": "fire_wood___the_cord",
  "title": "Fire Wood - the Cord",
  "description": "Calculate the number of cords in a pile of firewood by measuring length, width, and height. A cord is a standardized unit of stacked wood volume: 128 cubic feet or 3.62 cubic meters.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Fire Wood - the Cord\n\nThe cord is the most commonly used measurement unit for purchasing fuel wood.\n\nA cord is a stacked unit volume of wood where:\n- **1 cord = (4 ft) × (4 ft) × (8 ft) = 128 cubic feet**\n- **1 cord = (1.22 m) × (1.22 m) × (2.44 m) = 3.62 m³**\n\nThis volume includes bark and air space. Due to the irregular shape of wood, the air space in the cord can be as high as 40%. The net cord volume can therefore be as low as 75 cubic feet, with typical ranges of 80-100 cubic feet.\n\n### How to Calculate the Cords\n\nMeasure the **length (l)**, **width (w)**, and **height (h)** of the pile. Calculate the volume and divide by:\n- **128** if using feet\n- **3.62** if using meters"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "length",
          "label": "Length",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 12,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "width",
          "label": "Width",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2.5,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "height",
          "label": "Height",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 6,
          "unit": "ft"
        },
        {
          "id": "unit",
          "label": "Unit",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "feet",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Feet",
              "value": "feet"
            },
            {
              "label": "Meters",
              "value": "meters"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "volume",
          "label": "Total Volume",
          "formula": "inputs.length * inputs.width * inputs.height",
          "unit": "cubic feet / m³"
        },
        {
          "id": "cords",
          "label": "Number of Cords",
          "formula": "inputs.unit === 'feet' ? (inputs.length * inputs.width * inputs.height) / 128 : (inputs.length * inputs.width * inputs.height) / 3.62",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
